{"seconds": 360.5, "exit": 0, "final": "After **Bxg5 Nxf2+ Qxf2**:\n- White: captured g5 bishop (3) + captured f2 knight (3), lost f2 pawn (1) = net +5\n- This is winning!\n\n**So Bxg5 is the best move.** After all of Black's main tries:\n- **Nxf2+ Qxf2** wins material\n- **Ng3+ Qxg3** wins material  \n- **Nxg5 Nf7+** or other moves win material\n\n**Best move:** Bxg5\n\n**Main line:** Bxg5 Nxf2+ Qxf2 (or after Ng3+ Qxg3)\n\n**Motifs:** discoveredAttack, hangingPiece\n\n**Coaching note:**\n\n\"Look for undefended pieces\u2014the g5 bishop has no defender! After Bxg5, Black's e4 knight will give check or recapture, but in every case you emerge with extra material. If Nxf2+, you recapture with Qxf2 and you've won a bishop and knight for a pawn. If Ng3+ instead, Qxg3 wins both pieces. Always calculate forcing sequences when you spot a hanging piece: White wins material in all lines.\"\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Bxg5\", \"line\": [\"Bxg5\", \"Nxf2+\", \"Qxf2\"], \"motifs\": [\"hangingPiece\", \"discoveredAttack\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5p/p1p1p3/2PnNpb1/1P1Pn3/P4Q2/4BPPP/R1BR3K w - - 0 24"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5p/p1p1p3/2PnNpb1/1P1Pn3/P4Q2/4BPPP/R1BR3K w - - 0 24"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5p/p1p1p3/2PnNpb1/1P1Pn3/P4Q2/4BPPP/R1BR3K w - - 0 24", "square": "f3"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5p/p1p1p3/2PnNpb1/1P1Pn3/P4Q2/4BPPP/R1BR3K w - - 0 24", "square": "e5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5p/p1p1p3/2PnNpb1/1P1Pn3/P4Q2/4BPPP/R1BR3K w - - 0 24", "square": "g5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-square_info", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5p/p1p1p3/2PnNpb1/1P1Pn3/P4Q2/4BPPP/R1BR3K w - - 0 24", "square": "e4"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-square_info", "args": {"fen": "r1b1qrk1/1p5p/p1p1p3/2PnNpb1/1P1Pn3/P4Q2/4BPPP/R1BR3K w - - 0 24", "square